Author: anthnel <anthoni.devops@proton.me>
Date:   Tue Nov 10 13:18:43 2026 +0100

    fix: route pasted text to every focused field of the forge explorer (DEVDESK-201)

    The explorer's handlePaste only reached the table's filter bar. It now
    follows handleKeyMsg: table in edit mode, then the clone list filter bar,
    the creation form (name, description) and the "g" fuzzy finder. A paste
    never reaches the key handlers and is dropped when no field is focused.

    Also:
    - CRLF is normalized once in App.handlePasteMsg, so "a\r\nb" gives
      "a b" in every field (the fuzzy CRLF test moves to internal/app).
    - handlePaste no longer splits handleKeyMsg from its doc comment in
      explorer, jobsview, security and workspaces.
    - viewport guard: document its two limits, add a test that fails when
      it no longer sees helpViewport.Update, drop a redundant loop.

    Packages with a text field vs their tea.PasteMsg case:
func (m *Model) Update(msg tea.Msg) (tea.Model, tea.Cmd) {
	var cmd tea.Cmd

	switch msg := msg.(type) {
	case tea.WindowSizeMsg:
		m.width = msg.Width
		m.height = msg.Height

	case tea.KeyPressMsg:
		return m.handleKeyMsg(msg)

	case tea.PasteMsg:
		return m.handlePaste(msg)

	case AuthStartMsg:
		m.authenticating = true
		return m, m.spinner.Tick

	case AuthResultMsg:
		return m.handleAuthResult(msg)

